WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:09.074
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Jack Horton lives in San José in Costa Rica,

2
00:00:09.196 --> 00:00:12.760
where he teaches computer science at a secondary school.

3
00:00:14.058 --> 00:00:16.343
<v><b>Jack:</b></v> The first thing that I really noticed

4
00:00:16.343 --> 00:00:20.574
when I arrived here was how incredibly friendly the people are.

5
00:00:20.997 --> 00:00:25.962
The ‘ticos’ – that’s what they’re called – are much friendlier than people in Europe.

6
00:00:26.282 --> 00:00:29.996
They always say <i>buenos días</i> to you even if they don’t know you.

7
00:00:30.335 --> 00:00:37.284
And if something’s good, like a beautiful day or a good meal, they say <i>pura vida</i>, which I love.

8
00:00:37.444 --> 00:00:44.026
It literally means ‘pure life’, but I think it really means ‘things are great’, or something like that.

9
00:00:44.703 --> 00:00:47.655
One thing that can be difficult for foreigners though

10
00:00:47.721 --> 00:00:53.890
is that the sense of time is completely different in Costa Rica – they call it ‘tico time’.

11
00:00:54.332 --> 00:01:01.629
If there is an appointment at, let’s say, seven in the evening, ticos probably leave home at seven o’clock.

12
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.537
But everyone knows it’s OK not to arrive on time and it’s not a problem.

13
00:01:06.988 --> 00:01:13.740
Another thing that surprised me was the weather. I thought Costa Rica was hot and sunny all the time.

14
00:01:13.966 --> 00:01:19.946
That’s true in the dry season, and the temperature’s about twenty-five degrees all year round,

15
00:01:20.078 --> 00:01:28.409
but in the rainy season, especially in September and October, it rains really heavily for maybe two hours a day.

16
00:01:28.465 --> 00:01:31.719
Really amazing rain, nothing like in England.

17
00:01:32.151 --> 00:01:39.749
Everyone told me that the scenery was beautiful in Costa Rica, but it was even more beautiful than I expected.

18
00:01:39.806 --> 00:01:45.034
Incredible animals, birds, trees – and volcanoes.

19
00:01:45.203 --> 00:01:52.575
Some of them are active and smoke quietly, and then suddenly there’s a big bang and they start erupting.

20
00:01:52.707 --> 00:01:55.678
I was quite frightened the first time it happened.

21
00:01:56.111 --> 00:02:01.395
What else? Er, I thought that life here was going to be very cheap,

22
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:06.473
but in fact, food is very expensive, especially imported food.

23
00:02:06.736 --> 00:02:14.259
The only thing that’s cheap is fruit, vegetables, and coffee – wonderful, wonderful coffee.

24
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:19.243
And the fruit and vegetables are very different from what we have in Europe.

25
00:02:19.468 --> 00:02:24.433
One day I went to a market and I didn’t recognize any of the fruit.

26
00:02:25.054 --> 00:02:31.937
I like San José. Some people say it can be dangerous, but that’s true of most big cities.

27
00:02:32.031 --> 00:02:39.948
I don’t feel that it is. It is true that some of the roads are terrible, but in general, I really love it here.